style suggestion: do not rely on the DO variable 'i' after the loop
  --> tests/../integration_tests/do_variable_after_loop_01.f90:15:9
   |
15 |     if (i /= 11) error stop
   |         ^ after the loop, 'i' is 11
   |
12 |     do i = 1, 10
   |        ~ the loop sets 'i' here
   = help: the value is well defined, but it depends on how the loop ends and
           is easy to misread; inside the loop, assign the value you need to
           a variable with a meaningful name instead

style suggestion: do not rely on the DO variable 'j' after the loop
  --> tests/../integration_tests/do_variable_after_loop_01.f90:21:9
   |
21 |     if (j /= 3) error stop
   |         ^ 'j' has the value it had at the exit, or one step past the last iteration if the loop ends normally
   |
18 |     do j = 1, n
   |        ~ the loop sets 'j' here
   = help: the value is well defined, but it depends on how the loop ends and
           is easy to misread; inside the loop, assign the value you need to
           a variable with a meaningful name instead

